From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: use an identity domain for the MSM8998 MDSS

The bootloader leaves the panel scanning out its splash screen through
MMSS SMMU stream 0 in bypass. Since the IOMMU core attaches a default
domain as soon as the SMMU registers, even before the msm driver binds,
the MDSS got an empty translating domain: every MDP fetch faulted and
the resulting context fault interrupt storm stalled the whole boot.

Like the other Qualcomm display subsystems, let the MSM8998 MDSS keep
an identity mapping until the msm driver attaches its own domain.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -378,6 +378,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno-gmu" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdp4" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,qcm2290-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sar2130p-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc7180-mdss" },
